as a surprise bonus without cluttering the UI."},"1106":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-143","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#random-amount-ranges","content":"The `amount` field supports both fixed values and random ranges. To specify a range, use a table with two numbers: `{min, max}`."},"1107":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-144","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#random-amount-ranges","content":"When using random ranges, the preview UI will display the minimum value, but players will receive a random amount within the range when they actually open the lootbox."},"1108":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-145","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#custom-reward-types","content":"For rewards that aren't standard inventory items (vehicles, bank deposits, etc.), use the `rewardType` and `rewardData` fields along with the reward hook system."},"1109":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-146","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#custom-reward-types","content":"For custom reward types, the `name` field is just a **unique identifier** used for internal tracking and logging - it doesn't need to be an actual item in your inventory. Since custom rewards aren't real items, you must also provide `label` and `image` explicitly."},"1110":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-147","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#custom-reward-types","content":"Custom reward types require a registered reward hook to handle them. If no hook is registered, the system will fall back to default item behavior and log a warning."},"1111":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-148","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"When a player wins an item with a custom `rewardType`, the system looks for a registered hook for that type"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-149","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If a hook exists and returns `true`, the hook handled the reward"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-150","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If a hook returns `false`/`nil`, the system falls back to default item behavior"},"1114":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-151","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"If no hook exists, a warning is logged and the system falls back to default item behavior"},"1115":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-152","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#how-custom-rewards-work","content":"This ensures rewards are never silently lost - if something isn't configured correctly, players still receive items."},"1116":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-153","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#registering-reward-hooks","content":"Register hooks from your own resource to handle custom reward types:"},"1117":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-154","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#registering-reward-hooks","content":"See the Server Exports page for full API documentation."},"1118":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration-155","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/configuration#complete-vehicle-crate-example","content":"Here's a complete example of a lootbox that awards vehicles using custom reward types:"},"1119":